+### Name and evidence corrections
+
+- Vedic and VedicScript are one entry. The browser IDE is part of that ecosystem rather than a separately counted language here.
+- Vāk, Vāc, VakyaLang/Sansmatic and b7662777-hash's VĀKYA are distinct entries.
+- Rust package `karaka-core` and Joy Bose's KCC are separate projects.
+- `rainpaw/Sanskrit_Programming_Script` is the corrected source location.
+- SutraCode is not our Sutram repository.
+- ParamTatva's Sadhana/Sanskriti tools are separate from nickzq7's Sadhana and megaketu555's Sanskriti.
+- The academic Sanskritam paper is not evidence about every repository named Sanskritam.
+- Sanskriti's inspected implementation material gives more evidence than its earlier announcement alone. Conversely, an announced release date for Subhash does not establish an available release.
+- An inaccessible repository can be recorded as a lead, but cannot support claims about its implementation quality.
